# Reference reverse-proxy config for a real public deployment.
#
# This app has no public deployment target configured (see README) — this
# file is a starting point for when you have a server with a domain pointed
# at it. It is NOT wired into docker-compose.yml automatically: Caddy needs a
# real, publicly resolvable domain to request a Let's Encrypt certificate for,
# which isn't available in local/dev use.
#
# Usage once you have a domain and a server:
#   1. Point the domain's DNS A/AAAA record at your server.
#   2. Copy this file to Caddyfile (drop the .example) and replace
#      zyviora.example.com below with your real domain.
#   3. Run Caddy in front of the app, e.g. by adding a `caddy` service to
#      docker-compose.yml (image: caddy:2-alpine, ports 80/443, this file
#      mounted at /etc/caddy/Caddyfile, and a volume for its data/config so
#      certificates persist across restarts) on the same docker network as
#      the `web` service.
#   4. Set BEHIND_PROXY=true and SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE=true in .env — see
#      .env.example for why both matter.
#
# Caddy handles the Let's Encrypt certificate issuance and renewal
# automatically; there's no manual certbot/cron step.

zyviora.example.com {
    reverse_proxy web:5000
}
